/* =====================================================
   COMPOUND SELECTOR — DETAILED NOTES
   =====================================================

   1) What is a compound selector?
     A compound selector is a CSS selector made by combining multiple simple selectors without any spaces to target one single element that matches all the conditions.
      - Key: it targets *the same element* with multiple conditions.

   2) Syntax examples (basic):
      - tag + class:        div.card
      - class + class:      .btn.primary
      - id + class:         #header.big
      - tag + attribute:    input[type="email"]
      - class + pseudo:     a.button:hover
      - mixed:              button.btn.large[aria-pressed="true"]:focus

   3) How it works:
      - All simple selectors in the compound must be true for the
        same DOM element for the selector to match.
      - Order in the selector does NOT affect matching (but a
        conventional order improves readability).

   4) Conventional writing order (for readability, not required):
      tag → id → classes → attributes → pseudo-classes → pseudo-elements
      Example:  button#save.btn.primary[disabled]:focus::after

   5) Specificity (how CSS picks which rule wins):
      - ID selectors   => 100 points each
      - Class/attr/pseudo-class => 10 points each
      - Type/pseudo-element => 1 point each
      - Example:
         .card.large (10 + 10 = 20)
         #main (100)
         div.card (1 + 10 = 11)

   6) Compound vs combinator (difference):
      - Compound selector: `.menu.active`  → SAME element must have both classes.
      - Combinator selector: `.menu .item` → selects `.item` INSIDE `.menu` (different elements).
      - Compound = AND for one element. Combinator = relationship between elements.

   7) Examples (real use cases):

      /* target a bold primary button */
      button.btn.primary { padding: 12px 20px; }

      /* target required text inputs that are also styled */
      input.required[type="text"] { border: 2px solid blue; }

      /* target only focused link buttons */
      a.button:focus { outline: 2px solid #00f; }

      /* very specific — tag + class + attribute + pseudo-class */
      li.product[data-instock="true"]:first-child { font-weight: bold; }

   
   ===================================================== */
